      {
        "t": "h2",
        "x": "Questions We Get Most Often"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "How will I be able to keep my business open when the renovations are taking place?"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "Doing renovations after hours is a good way to keep the business open. Letting customers and employees know the plan and your schedule is critical so that employees are able to work before and after renovations. You will need to schedule some time when the business will be closed to complete major renovations. You may be able to do renovations in phases so that some areas remain open as others are closed."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "What do I do first before any work begins?"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "You need to start by having a solid plan. Planning means understanding what you want to do, how much money you can allocate to the plan (create a budget), and how long you estimate the work will take. This document would be critical for conversations with contractors to ensure they remain focused."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "Why do I need to consider how renovations affect day-to-day business operations?"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "Renovations can impact how your business operates. You may have to shuffle work locations, and people may have to occupy other positions for a while. Planning how the renovations may impact your employees and customers can help you mitigate and avoid negative operations impacts."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "Do I need to consider the future benefits of new renovations?"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "Yes, literally almost every business decision involves a consideration for return on investment (ROI). Investments such as roof replacements may incur immediate high costs, but lower future expenses, such as energy bills, and even increase your property value. Smart renovations with a delayed but substantial positive impact should be prioritized."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "What are some common issues that can delay renovations?"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "During renovations, things can go wrong. Unexpected issues, such as mold or old wiring, can arise. It is also possible for permitting to take longer than anticipated. Additionally, any changes in your plans, material delays, or scope changes can lead to delays."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "How do I choose the right contractor for my business renovation?"
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "x": "Choose a contractor with business renovation experience like yours. Ensure they communicate well, have knowledge of the local building codes, and can be problem-solvers. It is also beneficial to ask for samples of their previous work."
      }
